# MuseTalk Preprocessing Patch & Environment Fix

The goal is to replace the `mmpose` dependency in MuseTalk with `rtmlib` for better compatibility with Python 3.12 and modern environments. Additionally, we need to fix a NumPy version mismatch that's currently breaking `onnxruntime`.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The environment currently has NumPy 2.x, which is incompatible with many AI libraries like `onnxruntime` and `faster-whisper`. I will downgrade it to `1.26.4`.

## Proposed Changes

### Environment Fixes
- Downgrade `numpy` to `1.26.4` in the virtual environment.

### MuseTalk Patching
- **[MODIFY] [preprocess.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/tools/MuseTalk/scripts/preprocess.py)**:
  - Replace `mmpose` imports and model initialization with `rtmlib.Body`.
  - Update the `AnalyzeFace.__call__` method to use the `rtmlib` model and extract the same face landmark range (points 23-91).
- **[MODIFY] [preprocessing.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/tools/MuseTalk/musetalk/utils/preprocessing.py)**:
  - Similarly replace `mmpose` with `rtmlib.Body`.
  - Update `get_bbox_range` and `get_landmark_and_bbox` functions to use the new model.

